{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"All six life areas in one call (marriage, career, children, property, foreign, education), or the subset in `areas`. One chart and one dasha and transit scan shared; each area block equals its own /vedic/timing/{area} route. `level` defaults to antar here to keep the response small.\n\n[Group: Vedic]\n[Endpoint: POST /v1/vedic/timing/all]\n[Cost: 100 credits (Tier 4)]","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"body":{"allOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"description":"Birth data for a single natal chart. Required: date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:mm:ss), latitude and longitude in decimal degrees. The short forms lat, lon, lng and tz are rejected with 400 INVALID_FIELD; pass the full names. timezoneOffset is hours from UTC and defaults to 0, meaning UTC; send timezone instead (an IANA name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto) and the offset for that date is worked out, summer time included. city is a display label only: nothing here geocodes it, so it never stands in for coordinates. houseSystem is a single house-system letter, P by default; a name such as \"Placidus\" is refused, and the case matters because I and i are two different Sunshine systems.","properties":{"ayanamsa":{"description":"Sidereal school by name. Lahiri when omitted. Equivalent to ayanamsaId; send either.","enum":["fagan-bradley","lahiri","de-luce","raman","krishnamurti","kp","yukteshwar","jn-bhasin","true-citra","djwhal-khul"],"type":"string"},"ayanamsaId":{"type":["number","null"]},"city":{"default":"","type":"string"},"cosmogram":{"type":"boolean"},"date":{"pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"houseSystem":{"default":"P","enum":["P","K","R","C","E","W","B","M","O","A","T","V","D","F","G","H","I","i","L","N","Q","S","U","X","Y"],"type":"string"},"latitude":{"maximum":